  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "💍 Wedding Planner Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a wedding planner, coordinator or stylist, from Aisle Be There Weddings to Pour Toujours."
    },
    "intro": "Name your business with this **Wedding Planner Name Generator**: for wedding planners, on-the-day coordinators, wedding stylists and destination wedding planners. Pick a style and what you offer, or add your first name or town. Planning all kinds of events? Try the <a href=\"event-planning-business-name-generator.html\">Event Planning Business Name Generator</a>.",
    "sections": [],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "How do I check a wedding planner name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as two similar names nearby confuse customers."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should I call my business wedding planning or wedding coordination?",
        "answer": "Use the words for what you actually sell, because couples search for them. A wedding planner helps from the engagement to the day; a wedding coordinator (in the US often \"day-of\", in the UK \"on the day\") takes over in the last weeks and runs the day itself; a stylist does the look. If you might grow into full planning, a name ending in \"Weddings\" or \"Wedding Co.\" leaves room."
      }
    ]
  },
